    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020135": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Specified Purpose appointment (Estimated duration: approx. 5 year post - commencing in Sept. 2026 or shortly thereafter) Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production within the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science Applications are invited for the post of Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Dairy Production. This role, based in the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, will support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, and wider engagement in the area of dairy production. The appointee will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team of 18 full-time academics within the Section of Animal & Crop Science, contributing to a shared mission of addressing global food, environmental, and societal challenges through teaching, research, and knowledge exchange in animal and crop production systems. We are seeking a highly motivated individual with a demonstrated passion for teaching and research in dairy production, with an emphasis on grass-based systems of production. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in Agricultural Science or a closely related discipline, with a strong focus on dairy production and ideally with research interests that intersect with grass and forage production and environmental sustainability. In addition to a strong research profile, the appointee should demonstrate excellent communication, organisational and interpersonal skills and a commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020097": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2), UCD School of Politics and International Relations, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Politics and International Relations (x2) within UCD School of Politics and International Relations. The UCD School of Politics & International Relations (SPIRe) is a globally ranked, research-active school with teaching and research expertise across the fields of political science, international relations, normative political theory, international development, and other areas. It is committed to the highest standards in undergraduate and graduate teaching and research supervision. The school is home to a number of research centres, and further information can be found at: https://www.ucd.ie/spire/about/ 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 9th November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020090": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History, UCD School of History, Specified Purpose cover estimated duration 20 months Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor of Modern Migration History within the School of History The School of History is seeking to appoint a lecturer to a 1.5 year post in modern migration History. The School has recently expanded its teaching provision and research expertise in global and migration history. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing these teaching initiatives, pursue their own research projects and act as the academic lead on the School’s Summer School. The successful candidate will be expected to be in post for the 2026/27 Spring trimester (January 2027). Salary Scale: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) €66,055 - €104,600 Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020124": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Fixed-term post until 28 April 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Civil Engineering. The candidate will be involved with implementing high temporal resolution sampling strategies of key parameters (and proxy/ surrogate parameters) across selected study sites that reflect a full range of catchment pressures. In addition, the successful candidate will implement approaches to assess hydromorphological condition (or changes in condition) at these selected study sites. Event based sampling, where pollution releases will be at their highest will be systematically targeted. The candidate will analyse collected data and model studied catchments to inform more rapid and better decision making in the context of a pressure-stressor-response conceptual framework that will be explored. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020136": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Psychology, Fixed term 29th November 2029 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Psychology. Applications are invited from suitably qualified candidates for a full-time, fixed term position as a Postdoctoral Researcher with the School of Psychology, in collaboration with Jigsaw-The National Centre for Youth Mental Health. This position is funded by the Health Research Board (HRB) and is available from November 2026 until November 2029. Salary Scale: Post Doc Level 1 €47,273 - €52,513 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020118": {
      "title": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts",
      "description": "Recognition Events Manager, UCD Registry Student Recruitment & Recognition Events, Permanent, Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary posts Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Bainisteoir Imeachtaí Aitheantais laistigh de Clárlann UCD – Imeachtaí Earcaíochta agus Aitheantais Mac Léinn Cuireann Clárlann UCD réimse leathan seirbhísí riaracháin acadúla agus mac léinn ar fáil. Díríonn a misean ar sheirbhísí gairmiúla, treoir agus tacaíocht den scoth atá dírithe ar an mac léinn a fhorbairt agus a sholáthar do mhic léinn ionchasacha, do mhic léinn reatha, d’iar-mhic léinn, do bhaill foirne acadúla agus do bhaill foirne gairmiúla i ngach céim de shaolré mac léinn na hollscoile. Scála Tuarastail: €72,750 - €85,012 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 19/10/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Recognition Events Manager within UCD Registry – Student Recruitment & Recognition Events UCD Registry delivers a broad range of student and academic administrative services, whose mission is to develop and deliver the highest quality student-centred professional services, support and advice to prospective students, current students, alumni, faculty and professional staff in respect of the key administrative functions relating to a student's life cycle in the University. Salary: 95 Admin Off Ia_2013 (2010) (7080) €72,750 - €85,012 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19/10/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020116": {
      "title": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months",
      "description": "Research Business Development Manager, UCD School of Economics, 36 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Business Development Manager within UCD School of Economics. Rinn Energy is a national, co-led research centre funded by Research Ireland (Taighde Éireann), bringing together a consortium of leading universities and partners to deliver internationally leading, interdisciplinary research to support the transition to a low-carbon, secure, and resilient energy system. The Centre seeks to appoint a Business Development Manager (BDM) to successfully build collaborative research relationships between our world-leading academics and industry. The role requires identifying new industry members, projects, and training opportunities while maintaining a significant understanding of academic capabilities and industry requirements. The successful candidate will develop a portfolio of fully funded and co-funded collaborative research projects, with success measured directly by increased industry investment in the centre. Salary Scale: €88,000 - €105,000 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020119": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, 12 months (Temporary, Part-Time @ 0.5fte) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The EVEREST project is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Staff Exchange (MSCA SE) funded under Horizon Europe, focused on cutting-edge research into extracellular vesicles (EVs) for innovative diagnostic and therapeutic applications in oncology, cardiovascular, and neurodegenerative diseases. The Research Project Manager will play a key role in managing the project across its multiple partners in multiple countries, supporting the coordination of up to 285 months of secondments between academic and non-academic institutions. Salary: €40,000 - €50,000 per annum (€20,000 - €25,000 per annum pro rata) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020131": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy & Sports Sciences, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Part-Time 0.5FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor in Physiotherapy within the School of Public Health Supporting the UCD Director of Clinical Education, Subject Head, Programme Director(s) and Practice Education Team to deliver high quality academic and practice placement education. This position is aligned with Physiotherapy . The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will support staff on practice placement sites and the UCD Practice Education Team to deliver high quality practice placement education. The Special Lecturer/Clinical Tutor will also be available to support students virtually and/or in person if required by the UCD Practice Education Team. The appointee will contribute to module coordination and delivery for programmes offered by the school on-site in UCD and/or on-line where appropriate. The role will be based on site in UCD and/or on practice placement sites as directed by their line manager, with travel as required. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.5 FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 22 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020120": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary 5 years, Part-time (0.8 FTE), (Commencing on or before 01 January 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.8 FTE) post of a Teaching Fellow in Environmental Policy within UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy. The successful candidate will play a key role in the delivery and development of Environmental Policy teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate level, working across the Environmental Policy degree programmes to support high-quality, research-informed, policy-oriented, and experiential learning. The Teaching Fellow will contribute to the design, delivery and assessment of Environmental Policy modules, including through lectures, workshops, tutorials, project-based learning and other forms of skills-based teaching. In addition to the teaching duties, a particular focus of the role will be supporting module coordinators on modules with substantial student numbers, including teaching, administration and assessment of the modules. Overall, the Teaching Fellow will be expected to contribute to continuity of teaching provision across the Environmental Policy subject area. The post will have significant responsibilities in programme and student support, including module management, programme administration, management of online platforms, external-examiner support, supervision of postgraduate internships and research projects, as well as contributing to programme activities including orientation, careers and employer engagement. Fixed Salary: €49,500 Per Annum Pro-Rata (i.e. equal to €39,600 Per Annum, Part-time at 0.8 FTE) Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020059": {
      "title": "UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/10/2026 UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science Applications are invited for a very dynamic post-doctoral scientist to lead our Precision Nutrition, Obesity and Cancer Project within the Precision Oncology Ireland Programme (POI; https://www.precisiononcology.ie/) with Prof Helen Roche’s Nutrigenomics Team at UCD Conway Institute https://people.ucd.ie/helen.roche; in collaboration with Dr Martina Wallace and Dr Fiona McGillicdddy. POI, now in its second phase POI2, is a pioneering Irish consortium that brings together Irish universities, cancer charities, industry partners and healthcare providers to advance personalised cancer treatment. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020110": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Biomolecular & Biomedical Science. Applications are invited for a temporary, full-time position of Post-Doctoral Researcher in the UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, based in the Conway Institute. The lab is also linked with the FutureNeuro Research Centre (https://www.futureneurocentre.ie/). The successful applicant will work on a two-year research project exploring translational disruptions in mouse models of epilepsy. The postdoctoral researcher will use a combination of pharmacological and transgenic approaches, in vivo mouse models of epilepsy and molecular-based analyses to determine how altered translation contributes to epileptogenesis and seizure disorders. There will also be the opportunity for the researcher to explore and profile novel epitranscriptomic modifications in epilepsy. Examples of previous work can be found here: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=d2vwSvIAAAAJ&hl=en Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020048": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science, Temporary 18-month Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Researcher Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Biomolecular and Biomedical Science. The Chromatin Mechanisms in Disease laboratory (https://conwaychromatinlab.com/) at University College Dublin, led by Dr. Eric Conway, are recruiting a postdoctoral fellow to work on understanding the mechanisms through which the repressive histone modification H2AK119ub1 is dysregulated in disease. This position will be funded through a Wellcome Trust award. Histone H2A lysine 119 mono-ubiquitination (H2AK119ub1) is a repressive histone modification that is catalysed by the PRC1 complex and erased by the PR-DUB complex. Variants in critical subunits of each complex are known to be the causative event in diverse human diseases, such as AML and chromatinopathies. This project will investigate how pathogenic variants in members of the PRC1 and PR-DUB complexes contribute to changes in H2AK119ub1 using cancer and neurodevelopmental disease model systems. This will encompass a range of functional genomics, biochemistry and proteomics methods to investigate the precise impact that variants have on PR-DUB and PRC1 function – using methods such as CUT&Tag, Captify, RNA-seq, immunoprecipitation followed by mass spectrometry and high throughput pooled CRISPR screens. The role of the applicant will be either computational biology, wet-lab or a hybrid of both depending on the successful candidates expertise. There will be strong opportunities for continued professional development as part of UCD Research Careers Framework and through attendance at external training courses and conferences. The applicant will be strongly encouraged and supported to pursue external funding opportunities during the period of the appointment in line with the development of their own career prospects and to further the overall research activities of the group. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum PD2 Salary: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers who have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020138": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/12/2026 Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering within UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering The UCD School of Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering invites applications for the position of Associate Professor in Chemical and Bioprocess Engineering. The successful candidate will provide academic and research leadership, maintain and further develop an internationally recognised programme of research, attract competitive external funding, and supervise doctoral and postdoctoral researchers. They will contribute to high-quality teaching and project supervision at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including core subjects in the professionally accredited BE/ME programmes, and will play a substantive role in curriculum development, academic administration and School leadership. Research should complement or strengthen one or more of the School's priority areas: Pharmaceutical/Biopharmaceutical Engineering, Energy and the Environment, or Advanced Materials Engineering. The appointee will be expected to enhance the School's international profile and contribute to its academic, professional and wider societal impact. Application requirements: When preparing an application for this post, applicants should submit: A cover letter (no longer than three pages), A curriculum vitae and a list of publications. The cover letter should outline how the candidate meets the selection criteria and set out a forward-looking vision for their contribution at UCD, including their proposed research programme and external funding strategy, educational contribution, and approach to academic leadership. Where possible, applicants should include their ORCID. 95 Associate Professor_2010 Salary Scale: €85,864 - €121,260 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 11-Dec-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020154": {
      "title": "Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Temporary 12 months post - with the possibility of Extension",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Data Scientist II, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Temporary 12 months post - with the possibility of Extension Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Data Scientist II within UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR. CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. Salary Range: €55,000 - €70,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 21st October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020143": {
      "title": "Dispensary Veterinary Nurse, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Plus 12 Month Temporary Panel)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Dispensary Veterinary Nurse, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years (Plus 12 Month Temporary Panel) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Dispensary Veterinary Nurse within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine. UCD Veterinary Hospital (UCDVH) is seeking to appoint a veterinary nurse (career grade) (core) as part of the Dispensary Unit to provide a high standard of nursing care working within the team, fulfilling dispensary, prescription and stock requirements for hospital services. Particular to this position: You will be required to work 36.5 hours per week over 5 days during the week between Monday and Sunday. Weekend and weekday out-of-hours working may be required on a rota basis. Start and finish times will vary depending on the needs of the Hospital. The actual allocation of these hours of work will be arranged with your line manager. Vet Nurse_Career Grad (7928) Salary Scale: €38,255 - €49,021 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Altra Tréidliachta laistigh de Scoil an Leighis Tréidliachta UCD. Tá Ospidéal Tréidliachta UCD (UCDVH) ag iarraidh altra tréidliachta (grád gairme) (croílár) a cheapadh mar chuid den Aonad Íoclainne chun ardchaighdeán cúraim altranais a sholáthar ag obair laistigh den fhoireann, ag comhlíonadh riachtanais íoclainne, oidis agus stoic do sheirbhísí ospidéil. Go háirithe leis an seasamh seo: Beidh ort 36.5 uair a chloig a oibriú in aghaidh na seachtaine thar 5 lá i rith na seachtaine idir Dé Luain agus Dé Domhnaigh. D’fhéadfadh go mbeadh gá le deireadh seachtaine agus le hobair lasmuigh d’uaireanta oibre i rith na seachtaine ar bhonn róta. Beidh amanna tosaithe agus críochnaithe éagsúil ag brath ar riachtanais an Ospidéil. Socrófar leithdháileadh iarbhír na n-uaireanta oibre seo le do bhainisteoir líne. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 23 Mí Deireadh Fomhair 2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020141": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary Fixed Term 3 year contract or Permanent post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary Fixed Term 3 year contract or Permanent post Applications are invited for a temporary or permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Crop Science within UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science The appointee will join the Animal and Crop Science Section and will contribute to both undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, conduct high quality research in Crop Science and engage in associated administrative tasks. The appointee will join a highly motivated and research active Crop Science team who are involved with teaching and research in areas including principles of crop science, cereal production, root and alternative crops, grassland, plant health, organic agriculture, digital agriculture and bioenergy. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 23-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020145": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 1 Year (Part-Time 0.4 FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 1 Year (Part-Time 0.4 FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology and Equine Internal Medicine within the School of Veterinary Medicine. This is a temporary post as Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Veterinary Physiology (0.2FTE) and Equine Internal Medicine (0.2FTE) based in the School of Veterinary Medicine, UCD. This split post sits within the Sections of “Veterinary Biosciences” and “Equine Clinical Studies, Diagnostic Imaging and Anaesthesia”, and the appointee will be expected to significantly enhance the existing team within both sections. Applicants must be in possession of a degree in veterinary medicine registrable with the Veterinary Council of Ireland (www.vci.ie) 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 – €104,600 per annum Pro Rata @ 0.4FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information, please follow the link: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020152": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Architecture, Planning & Environmental Policy, Temporary 36 months post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Architecture, Planning & Environmental Policy, Temporary 36 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within the School of Architecture A 36-month post-doctoral position is available in the UCD School of Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy in the area of rural planning, rural development, local regeneration and demographic changes. ‘REROOTED’ (Resilient European rural outlooks: opportunities for transformation, empowerment and development) is a Horizon Europe funded project involving an international collaboration involving universities from Ireland, the Netherlands, Italy, Denmark, Greece and Estonia, along with partners in practice, to examine rural demographic changes and strategies for rural regeneration. The project is interdisciplinary, comprising research methods spanning quantitative and qualitative approaches. Specifically, this post-doctoral position will assist with project workpackages related to (1) understanding driving forces and impacts of rural demographic trends; (2) evaluating national and regional strategies for addressing demographic changes; and (3) exploring local innovation strategies. This work will also involve primary research based in rural Ireland and collaborating closely with local groups. The appointed person will be responsible for key deliverables, data gathering and analysis, report writing and project dissemination. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. PD1 Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum PD2 Salary Range: €55,399 - €56,957 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020156": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 24 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2 within UCD School of Earth Sciences. This postdoctoral position is part of the ROTTnROCK project, funded by a European Research Council Synergy grant (http://rottnrock.org). Candidates with expertise in numerical modelling, particularly Finite Element Method modelling, and thermal or fluid coupling are encouraged to apply. The position will be funded for 24 months, with opportunity for extension. Funding will also be supplied for computing, fieldwork, attendance at conferences and workshops, and publication fees. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum ; PD2 Salary Scale : €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum** Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 04/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020153": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD Mathematics and Statistics, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD Mathematics and Statistics, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within the School of Mathematics and Statistics We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to join the School of Mathematics and Statistics at University College Dublin (UCD). The position is funded by the Centre for Artificial Intelligence in Weather Forecasting and Climate Change, a collaboration between UCD and Met Éireann. The postdoctoral researcher will be co supervised by meteorologists from Met Éireann’s Research and Application Division. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting edge research focused on the statistical post processing of raw numerical weather prediction (NWP) output to correct known model biases. Bias corrected output will provide more accurate forecasts, delivering significant downstream benefits for forecasters and for applications that rely on NWP output. The project is therefore central to a wide range of weather-related services provided by Met Éireann. It will contribute to improving the accuracy and reliability of forecasts delivered through Met Éireann’s website and app, third party services, and weather warnings, and aligns closely with Met Éireann’s overall strategy. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020148": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 18 months post",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 18 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Postdoctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering. NanoMind-GenAI is an ARC-ICT funded project on the development of a AI driven formulation and manufacturing software platform for lipid nanoparticles with the applications towards RNA therapeutics. NanoMind-GenAI will deliver an AI-driven decision-support platform that closes this gap. Combining agent-supported literature retrieval and interpretation with machine learning validated on over 3,000 LNP formulations, the platform will generate explainable, evidence-based formulation recommendations, supporting faster and more knowledge-grounded candidate prioritisation with traceable reasoning. Expected outputs include a tested software workflow, evidence-based candidate prioritisation methods, research publications and contributions to the project’s commercial development. This is a research focused role, where you will conduct a specified programme of research supported by research training and development under the supervision and direction of a Principal Investigator. Salary range: €47,273 - €49,890 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020139": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Music, 18 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Music, 18 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Music. The School of Music at University College Dublin is launching a new postdoctoral fellowship competition for outstanding early-career researchers working in any area of music research. The scheme is intended to provide career development opportunities for leading music researchers at an early stage of their careers while further enriching the lively research culture of the School. This post runs alongside our existing commitment to – and success in – supporting candidates for externally-funded schemes such as Government of Ireland and MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowships. The Fellowship will last 18 months and will provide extensive research time and support; successful candidates will also have the opportunity to gain teaching experience. The fellowship will start on 01 January 2027. Salary: €47,273 per annum . Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 01/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020146": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 7 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 7 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands within UCD School of Earth Sciences. Applications are invited from suitably qualified persons for the post of Research Assistant in Remote Sensing of Peatlands at University College Dublin (UCD). The post will be based at the Irish Centre for Research in Applied Geosciences (iCRAG), which is hosted at UCD School of Earth Sciences. The post will involve extensive collaboration with colleagues within iCRAG and at CeADAR, the national centre for applied data analytics and Artificial Intelligence. Research Assistant Salary Scale: €34,129 - €43,227 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020142": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, School of Earth Sciences, 2 years until maximum 31st December 2028",
      "description": "Research Assistant, School of Earth Sciences, 2 years until maximum 31st December 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within School of Earth Sciences . The Research Assistant will be primarily responsible for the day to day running of (1) a Bruker M4 Tornado+ microXRF machine for analysis of thin section, core and hand samples, and (2) our Multi Sensor Core Logger instrument, a Geotek MSCL-S which scans various sizes of drill core: this will be installed in Q4 2026. You will contribute to data collection across several projects in economic geology and raw materials in the School. In addition, the post holder will contribute to geothermal projects, acquiring and preparing representative core and rock samples from typical geological regions in Ireland, characterising their thermo-hydraulic properties, and supporting the School’s petrographic laboratories. The role involves fieldwork at sites and core stores across the Republic of Ireland, and the successful candidate must be willing to travel and to work in the field as required. This position will be a key part of the large team working on sedimentary basin research in Ireland and globally in the School of Earth Sciences. Research Assistant Salary: €34,129 - €38,102 per annum (Research Assistant points 1 – 6) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 03/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020150": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 9 months (Part-Time 0.5FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 9 months (Part-Time 0.5FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Medicine. Applications are invited for a research assistant to support the ECHO study, a prospective observational cohort examining childhood health outcomes following maternal e-cigarette use. The study follows mothers and their babies from pregnancy to two years of age and examines growth, respiratory and neurobehavioural development. The impact of vaping during pregnancy on childhood health outcomes is currently unknown and this is the first study in the world to ever examine these outcomes longitudinally over the first two years of life. Salary Range: €34,129 - €36,272 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.5 FTE. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020103": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 6 Months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 6 Months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within the School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, is currently seeking to appoint a highly motivated research assistant to contribute to a funded project titled End of Life care in Nursing Homes The successful candidate will play a crucial role the experience of staff providing end-of-life care in nursing homes, particularly focusing on the development and deployment data collection tools, support with data analysis, creation of publications, and development of conference presentations. Salary Range: €34,129 - €35,395 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 19 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020151": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Geography, 36 months (Temporary part time)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Geography, 36 months (Temporary part time) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Geography. The Research Project Manager will specifically support two recently awarded European Research Council (ERC) Grant awardees, projects MigHealthGaps, and HERDPATH. The position is part-time at 50% and provides the opportunity for a suitable candidate to gain valuable experience working in UCD supporting two research leaders in all aspects of ERC research management and administration. Salary: €47,489 (@0.51282 fte pro rata) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27th October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020149": {
      "title": "Robotics Research Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post",
      "description": "Robotics Research Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Robotics Research Engineer within UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Funded by Horizon Europe’s European Innovation Council Patherfinder programme, the CEREBRIS project aims to revolutionise how neurological conditions are monitored and managed. By combining brain signals, imaging, movement and clinical data, CEREBRIS aims to support earlier diagnosis, more precise prognosis to transform personalised care. Salary: €38,000 - €48,000 annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27-10-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020159": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital), UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028",
      "description": "Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital), UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer / Clinical Tutor in Neonatology (The National Maternity Hospital) within UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital. The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. A number of Clinical Tutors are also actively involved in our biomedical, clinical or medical education research working with a specific Principal Investigator and may be undertaking a higher research degree (e.g. MD, MCh, MAO, MSc or PhD). These individuals are responsible for undertaking research experiments or data reviews and disseminating their findings through publication as a thesis, in academic journals or at scientific meetings. All Clinical Tutors are part of a vibrant community of academic staff who pass on their clinical experience and expertise to the next generation of medical professionals. The School provides academic support and training such that the Tutors themselves develop their own educational expertise and leadership. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 29/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020163": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital, UCD School of Medicine National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital, UCD School of Medicine National Maternity Hospital, Temporary Fixed Term 12 months from 12th July 2027 to 9th July 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, The National Maternity Hospital within UCD School of Medicine / National Maternity Hospital The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 30-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020147": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland, Temporary 1 year",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland, Temporary 1 year Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Medicine/Systems Biology Ireland. Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Research Fellow position to support a programme of work on early onset colorectal cancer. Based within the Research Groups of Dr Oleksii Rukhlenko and Prof. David Gomez Matallanas in Systems Biology Ireland (SBI) at UCD, the Postdoctoral Research Fellow will contribute to the ambitious Precision Oncology Ireland 2 (POI-2) Programme, which is coordinated by SBI and brings together researchers across multiple institutions. The role requires (1) knowledge of bioinformatics, (2) extensive hands-on experience in analysis of omics data, (3) some practical experience in multi-omics integration and network biology, (4) understanding of cancer biology and systems biology. About the Precision Oncology Ireland Programme: Precision Oncology Ireland (POI; https://www.precisiononcology.ie/) is a pioneering Irish consortium that brings together Irish universities, cancer charities, industry partners and healthcare providers to advance personalised cancer treatment. Coordinated by Systems Biology Ireland at UCD, POI leverages systems biology approaches to analyse complex molecular data and understand cancer at a deeper level. By integrating multiomics data, imaging, and clinical data through computational modelling, the consortium aims to tailor therapies to individual patients' tumour profiles. POI is working to improve diagnostics, reduce unnecessary treatments, and accelerate the development of targeted cancer therapies. PD1 Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. PD2 Fixed Salary: €55,399 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers who have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020155": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, in association with UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics, is advertising an exciting research position as part of a cross-border project using epidemiological modelling to inform sustainable control of bovine tuberculosis on the Island of Ireland. The Post-doctoral Research Fellow will develop and implement mechanistic and statistical modelling tools, tapping the experience of a strongly interdisciplinary research team, to better target interventions to control tuberculosis in Irish cattle. Post-doctoral level 1 or 2 Salary Scale: €47,273 – €53,925 per annum or €55,399 - €60,250 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 11-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020161": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology, Temporary 36 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology, Temporary 36 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Medicine - Charles Institute of Dermatology. The ECM lab led by Associate Professor Seungkuk Ahn at University College Dublin in Ireland has an opening for a Postdoctoral Research position (PD level 1) to work on the ERC-funded “DESIGN-ECM” project to investigate the role of species and sex of extracellular matrix and cells for better designing 3D tissue models. Human mimetic preclinical models imitate human organs, tissues, and diseases to enable safer, more accurate testing for new drugs and therapies. Such models are created by employing core biomaterials and cells existing in our tissues. These models have significant potential to enhance our understanding of human disease and the development of treatments. However, the majority of human preclinical models to date have neglected the species and sex of the extra cellular matrix and cells as biological variables, while species- and sex-dependent biomaterial and cell properties have been well acknowledged in animal and clinical studies. Led by Dr Seungkuk Ahn, DESIGN-ECM will address this gap by investigating species-driven dimorphism in biomaterials and cell biology across various disciplines such as materials science, bioengineering, organoids, mechanobiology, nanobiotechnology. Success in this project will reshape the design of future preclinical models to seriously reckon with species and sex of biomaterials and cells, moving towards personalised tissue models in the long term. Candidates will work together with 2 PhD students to establish the core methodologies and data sets for the first 36 months of the total 60-month ERC project. The main scientific works will 1) engineer and characterise 3D ECM scaffolds, 2) perform in vitro cell validations, and 3) develop 3D ovarian organoid models. The start date of this position is 01 May 2027. Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 05 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020157": {
      "title": "Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI, Temporary 12-month post(s)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/10/2026 Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI, Temporary 12-month post(s) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Work Ready Graduate Data Scientist x 12 within the School of Computer Science Are you interested in becoming an applied AI/data scientist and developing a career in the world’s fastest growing and arguably most exciting discipline of AI/data analytics? Then this ‘work-ready’ graduate training programme may be a great opportunity for you. CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI is running the next phase of the Work Ready Graduate Programme for 2027 from January 2027 to December 2027. Work Ready Trainee Graduates are hosted both at CeADAR and at one of our industry partners offices. CeADAR is recruiting 12 Work Ready Graduate candidates with solid coding experience and with a postgraduate degree in a numerate subject such as Computer Science, Data Analytics, AI, Engineering or Maths/Statistics. Eligible candidates must hold a completed Master’s qualification from a university or accredited higher education institution. CeADAR, based in University College Dublin, is funded by Enterprise Ireland to support companies in embracing and leveraging AI technology. CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland. The applied research at CeADAR covers broad aspects of AI and data analytics using advanced machine learning to deal with structured and unstructured data coming from many different sectors. This is an exciting opportunity to be involved in this strategic and nationally important area of AI where CeADAR is shaping the strategy at the national and EU level. Fixed Salary: €38,885 per annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 28 October 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020173": {
      "title": "Asia Executive Assistant, Temporary 2 year post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Asia Executive Assistant, Temporary 2 year post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Asia Executive Assistant within NUI Dublin Pte in Singapore. This post is a temporary 2-year contract based in Singapore. The appointee will be an employee of NUI Dublin Pte in Singapore. NUI Dublin Pte is a subsidiary of UCD. UCD College of Business is a dynamic business school located in the vibrant European capital of Dublin. Consistently ranked amongst the leading business schools in the world, the College of Business is currently ranked 23rd in the Financial Times European Business Schools rankings. It is the only Irish member of the Global Alliance in Management Education (CEMS) and the Global Network for Advanced Management (GNAM), and also holds the triple crown of accreditation from AACSB (US), EQUIS (Europe) and AMBA (UK). The College comprises of the Lochlann Quinn School of Business (Quinn School), the Michael Smurfit Graduate Business School (Smurfit School), the Global Campus (GC) and Smurfit Executive Development (SED). The Quinn School and GC are located on the main campus at Belfield while the Smurfit School and SED are located on the Blackrock campus. UCD College of Business GC has a significant overseas presence in Singapore. This post will be based in Singapore. The appointee will be an employee of NUI Dublin Pte in Singapore. Salary range: €30,000 - 45,000 per annum. Closing date: 17:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13th of November 2026. To apply, please submit an application via this google form link: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdX2dSI90B_Xj9HC4CB2RV37U1U5gpSMEE7aR_qXZuQz4N5ng/viewform?usp=header Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020175": {
      "title": "Chief Analyst, Medical Bureau of Road Safety, Permanent (Permanent (12 month Permanent Panel)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 17/11/2026 Chief Analyst, Medical Bureau of Road Safety, Permanent (Permanent (12 month Permanent Panel) Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Chief Analyst within the Medical Bureau of Road Safety The Medical Bureau of Road Safety (Bureau) has statutory responsibilities for the chemical testing for intoxicants in driving and related functions. The functions of the Bureau are laid down in the Road Traffic Acts and include receipt and analysis for intoxicants of specimens of blood and urine forwarded to the MBRS; Issuing of Certificates of Analysis; provision of equipment for the taking or provision of specimens of blood and urine; research on alcohol and drugs in relation to driving and development of forensic toxicology methods; approval, supply and testing of equipment or apparatus for determining the presence of drugs in oral fluid and approval, supply and testing of equipment or apparatus for indicating The Chief Analyst in the Medical Bureau of Road Safety is considered to be one of the leading and significant forensic scientists in Ireland playing a key role in the delivery of the functions of the Bureau under the Road Traffic Acts. This role is a highly specialised position as it requires the relevant qualifications in a direct relevant discipline, appropriate high level of experience both with in the areas of science and law. The ability to demonstrate integrity, a commitment to excellence, develop and expand scientific programmes for current and future Road Traffic Acts is an essential prerequisite for this position. Salary Scale: 95 Snr Administrative Ii_2013 (2010) (7075) €112,235 - €150,022 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 17 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Príomh Anailísí laistigh de An Lia-Bhiúró um Shábháilteacht ar Bhóithre Tá freagrachtaí reachtúla ar an Lia-Bhiúró um Shábháilteacht ar Bhóithre (an Lia-Biúró) maidir le tástáil cheimiceach le haghaidh meisceoirí i dtiomáint agus feidhmeanna gaolmhara. Leagtar síos feidhmeanna an Lia-Bhiúró sna hAchtanna um Thrácht ar Bhóithre agus áirítear leo samplaí fola agus fuail a chuirtear ar aghaidh chuig an Lia-Bhiúró a fháil agus anailís a dhéanamh orthu le haghaidh meisceoirí; Teastais Anailíse a Eisiúint; trealamh a sholáthar chun samplaí fola agus fuail a thógáil nó a sholáthar; taighde ar alcól agus drugaí i ndáil le tiomáint agus forbairt modhanna tocsaineolaíochta fóiréinseacha; trealamh nó fearas a cheadú, a sholáthar agus a thástáil chun láithreacht drugaí i sreabhán béil a chinneadh agus trealamh nó fearas a cheadú, a sholáthar agus a thástáil chun comharthaí a léiriú. Meastar gurb é an Príomh Anailísí sa Lia-Bhiúró ar dhuine de na heolaithe fóiréinseacha is suntasaí agus is mó le rá in Éirinn agus ról lárnach acu i gcomhlíonadh fheidhmeanna an Bhiúró faoi na hAchtanna um Thrácht ar Bhóithre. Mar phost an-speisialaithe, éilíonn sé cáilíochtaí foirmiúla i ndisciplín gaolmhar go díreach mar aon le taithí fhairsing a chlúdaíonn réimsí eolaíocha agus dlíthiúla araon. I measc na gceanglais lárnacha don ról, tá an cumas chun ionracas a léiriú, tiomantas don sármhaitheas, agus an cumas chun tionscnaimh eolaíocha a bhunú agus a leathnú atá ailínithe le reachtaíocht tráchta ar bhóithre reatha agus amach anseo. 95 Snr Administrative Ii_2013 (2010) (7075) Scála Tuarastail: €112,235 - €150,022 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 17.11.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020165": {
      "title": "Clinical Tutor in Mental Health Nursing, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 5 Years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/11/2026 Clinical Tutor in Mental Health Nursing, UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems, Temporary Fixed Term 5 Years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Clinical Tutor in Mental Health Nursing within UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems. University College Dublin is a research-intensive and globally engaged university and is No. 1 in Ireland in the QS Graduate Employability rankings. The UCD School of Nursing, Midwifery and Health Systems is a constituent School of the UCD College of Health and Agricultural Sciences. The School is a national provider of undergraduate and postgraduate registration education programmes in nursing and midwifery and graduate-taught programmes in health systems and health professions’ education. Its programmes emphasise clinical expertise, critical inquiry, leadership development, personal growth, communication, teamwork, interprofessional collaboration, and lifelong learning. The School is a leading research-intensive school with a large portfolio of programmatic and single-project research. UCD Nursing is ranked in the 44th in the QS World Subject Rankings. The School wishes to appoint a Clinical Tutor in Mental Health Nursing to support the delivery of its registration education programmes in Mental Health Nursing. The Clinical Tutor will be responsible for teaching of mental health nursing in a range of settings, including the simulation laboratory, the practice setting, the classroom, and the virtual learning environment, and will use a range of classroom and online teaching methods to facilitate the effective integration of students’ academic and clinical studies. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 02 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020172": {
      "title": "Design Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary part-time (i.e. 0.3 FTE) appointment for 5 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Design Fellow in Environmental Policy, UCD School Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy, Temporary part-time (i.e. 0.3 FTE) appointment for 5 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Design Fellow in Environmental Policy within the School Architecture, Planning and Environmental Policy Applications are invited for a temporary five-year, 0.3FTE, post of Design Fellow in Environmental Policy. The Design Fellow contact is a Seasonal Part-time contract whereby the Design Fellow will work over 27 weeks of the year. This post is aimed at experienced practitioners in the field. The successful applicant will engage in teaching in studio, lectures and workshops. Applicants must have a graduate degree in environmental policy or a related area, have strong credentials in environmental policy and suitable teaching expertise. Overall, the Design Fellow will be expected to contribute to continuity of teaching provision across the Environmental Policy subject area. Please note, this recruitment process will be used to create a panel which may be used to fill subsequent temporary Design Fellow appointments, if any, arising in the next twelve months. 95 Administrative Officer 1 (2010) Salary Scale: €53,876 - €72,929 per annum, pro-rata [Equal to €8,392 - €11,867 annually, working 27wks of the year (part-time) at 0.3FTE] Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020177": {
      "title": "Facilities Assistant – temporary part time, UCD Library , Fixed term 15 May 2027",
      "description": "Facilities Assistant – temporary part time, UCD Library , Fixed term 15 May 2027 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Facilities Assistant – temporary part time within UCD Library. The role involves maintaining the library as a safe and secure place to study. This includes opening/closing the library and monitoring the public areas to ensure that library regulations are followed by all users. This is a varied role and full training will be given to successful candidates. 95 Services Steward_2013 (7931) €37,108 - €46,380 at 0.3fte pro rata. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 28/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020185": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor (Systemic Psychotherapy), School of Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 48 months (Part-Time 0.6FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor (Systemic Psychotherapy), School of Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 48 months (Part-Time 0.6FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor (Systemic Psychotherapy) within the School of Medicine The UCD School of Medicine has an international reputation as a centre of excellence in the domain of psychotherapy. The School of Medicine offers an extensive portfolio of graduate opportunities at Higher Diploma, Graduate Diploma, Masters, Professional Masters and Doctoral level across four major specific modalities of psychotherapy, namely, Child Art Psychotherapy, Group Analytic Psychotherapy, Psychoanalytic Psychotherapy, and Systemic Psychotherapy. Lecturers are experienced clinicians in the specific modality with considerable academic expertise related to their specific modality of psychotherapy. There is professional body recognition in place for each of the specific modalities of psychotherapy of the UCD Professional Masters programmes. The Masters programmes are first and foremost clinical training programmes. Academic research is a core component of the Professional Masters Programmes and informs the teaching of both theoretical and clinical practice modules . UCD Psychotherapy is engaging with the consultation processes of CORU, the Health and Social Care Professions Regulator, which is currently occupied with the operationalising of the State Board with responsibility for the regulation of the titles Counsellor and Psychotherapist in Ireland. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.6FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 5 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020179": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Mathematics, UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics, Permanent (Commencing on 1 September 2027)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Mathematics, UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics, Permanent (Commencing on 1 September 2027) Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Mathematics within UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics. The School of Mathematics and Statistics at University College Dublin is seeking to appoint a permanent Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Mathematics. Applicants from all areas of Mathematics are invited to apply; however preference may be given to candidates whose research is in the areas of algebra, discrete mathematics, geometry and number theory, broadly interpreted. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and sustain a leading research programme in mathematics, including publishing in peer-reviewed academic journals, the supervision of research students and the development and submission of competitive applications for external funding. The candidate will be expected to develop a research programme that broadens and integrates with current areas of mathematics research expertise in the School. The successful candidate will also be expected to be committed to pursuing excellence in undergraduate and postgraduate teaching across the School’s wide-ranging programmes, and to contribute to the development and delivery of new programmes. The UCD School of Mathematics and Statistics is the largest of its kind in Ireland and has over 70 academic staff from all areas of mathematics and statistics. Research activities in the School are supported by a variety of sources including the €460M Research Ireland grant for Rinn AI, Centre for Research and Innovation in Data Science and AI, supporting 258 PhD students nationwide,the €22M Research Ireland Centre for Research Training in the Foundations of Data Science (https://www.data-science.ie/) which currently has 19 PhD students in UCD, Met Eireann and Google for the research centre Aimsir, and through European Union funding, e.g., the European Research Council (ERC) and Doctoral Training Network schemes. Individual fellowships held by members of the School over the last few years include three ERC Advanced Grants, two IRC Advanced Laureate Awards, two Royal Society/Research Ireland University Research Fellowships, as well as SFI-IRC Research Council Pathway Fellowships and Marie Skłodowska-Curie Action Postdoctoral Fellowships. The School has strong research links with a broad variety of industry and enterprise partners. The School also has internally funded research support schemes and PhD scholarships. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 – €104,600 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 16 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information, please follow the link: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020191": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Physical Geography, UCD School of Geography, Temporary Fixed Term 3-year post",
      "description": "Closing Date: 14/12/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Physical Geography, UCD School of Geography, Temporary Fixed Term 3-year post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Physical Geography within the School of Geography The UCD School of Geography invites applications for a 3-year Lecturer/Assistant Professor position in Physical Geography. We seek an outstanding scholar with a strong research profile, or clear potential to develop one, in any area of physical geography, including but not limited to geomorphology, hydrology, climatology, biogeography, Quaternary and environmental change, Earth and planetary surface processes, or related field-based, laboratory, geospatial or modelling approaches. The successful candidate will contribute to internationally recognised research, seek and attract external research funding, and help strengthen and further develop Physical Geography within the School. The appointee will have the opportunity to make use of, and contribute to the further development of, the School’s new state-of-the-art Physical Geography Laboratory, which provides an important platform for field-, laboratory- and methods-based research and teaching. The appointee will also be expected to deliver engaging and high-quality teaching, inspire students, develop modules at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, supervise research students, and contribute to field-based and practical methods training where appropriate. We particularly welcome applicants whose work engages with pressing geographical questions concerning environmental change, landscape dynamics, climate-related processes, human–environment interactions, or the physical processes shaping places and regions. The appointee will also contribute to School, College and University service, and to an inclusive and collegial academic community. Salary Scale: 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) - €66,055 - €104,600 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 14 December 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020183": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor, Systemic Psychotherapy, UCD School of Medicine,  Temporary Fixed Term 48 months, Part-Time 0.4FTE",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor, Systemic Psychotherapy, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 48 months, Part-Time 0.4FTE Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor (Systemic Psychotherapy)within UCD School of Medicine The UCD School of Medicine has an international reputation as a centre of excellence in the domain of psychotherapy. The School of Medicine offers an extensive portfolio of graduate opportunities at Higher Diploma, Graduate Diploma, Masters, Professional Masters and Doctoral level across four major specific modalities of psychotherapy, namely, Child Art Psychotherapy, Group Analytic Psychotherapy, Psychoanalytic Psychotherapy, and Systemic Psychotherapy. Lecturers are experienced clinicians in the specific modality with considerable academic expertise related to their specific modality of psychotherapy 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 Per Annum Pro Rata @ 0.4FTE Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 05-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information please follow link below: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020171": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Temporary 12 months post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering. Post-doctoral Research Fellow – Real-Time Decoding of Motor Unit Activity for Clinical Applications Applications are invited for a 1-year post-doctoral position with the Neuromuscular Systems Research Lab at University College Dublin. The project represents an exciting opportunity to work on a multidisciplinary research project as part of the Research Ireland RINN AI Centre. A highly motivated post-doctoral research fellow is sought to lead the development of methods for real-time decoding of motor unit activity for clinical applications including Parkinson’s disease. The project would suit candidates with expertise in electromyography (EMG), high density EMG, motor unit analysis, neural signal analysis and computational modelling. Fixed Salary: €47,273 per annum. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020176": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, 12 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, 12 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development and implementation of a platform trial infrastructure in general practice. The work builds on established national and European collaborations in general practice research and clinical trials, including collaboration with ECRAID and the ECRAID-Prime network. The post will have a strong implementation and operational focus. The successful candidate will work with participating general practices, European research partners and trial teams to support the implementation and delivery of platform trials in general practice. A particular focus will be on developing efficient approaches to participant identification, recruitment, trial monitoring and data collection using routinely collected data from general practice patient management systems. PD1 Salary Scale: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum . Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 03/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020174": {
      "title": "Professor and Deputy Principal GDIC, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science OR UCD School of Biology & Environmental Science (permanent and ongoing), UCD Guangzhou-Dublin International College of Life Sciences & Technology (GDIC) at South China Agricultural University (for the first 5 years of tenure only)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 17/11/2026 Professor and Deputy Principal GDIC, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science OR UCD School of Biology & Environmental Science (permanent and ongoing), UCD Guangzhou-Dublin International College of Life Sciences & Technology (GDIC) at South China Agricultural University (for the first 5 years of tenure only) Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Professor and Deputy Principal GDIC within UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science OR UCD School of Biology & Environmental Science (permanent and ongoing) AND UCD Guangzhou-Dublin International College of Life Sciences & Technology (GDIC) at South China Agricultural University (for the first 5 years of tenure only). This is a full-time permanent academic post. The appointee will become an academic associated with one of the UCD constituent Schools of GDIC, either the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science or the UCD School of Biology & Environmental Science, through which they will manage their research and teaching activities under the remit of their Head of School. For the first 5 years of their appointment the appointee will also serve as Deputy Principal of GDIC. The reporting line for their Deputy Principal GDIC duties will be to the Principal GDIC. The Head of School and the Principal GDIC will work collaboratively to achieve an appropriate balance of duties within the parameters of a normal academic workload of teaching & learning, research and administrative duties. We are seeking a candidate who will work with colleagues to deliver modules in our undergraduate and taught graduate degree programmes (either at GDIC or in Dublin), supervise undergraduate and taught graduate research projects and support the Principal GDIC in providing academic oversight and leadership for programmes offered at GDIC. The successful candidate will be research active with a track record of excellence in teaching and research commensurate Professor level at UCD. Particular to this position: Given the nature of the role a commitment to spending time at GDIC in Guangzhou is required. External appointees, or internal appointees currently teaching on GDIC programmes, will spend one Teaching Semester at GDIC and also spend up to six weeks, but no less than 3 weeks, including the first 3 weeks of the semester in the opposite semester to their teaching semester at GDIC. Internal appointees currently fulfilling their teaching commitments on campus in Dublin, will spend six weeks per semester, including the first 3 weeks of each semester, at GDIC with existing on campus academic duties adjusted to suit. 95 Professor (7939) Salary Scale: €106,611 - €142,500 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 17 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Note: Hours of work for academic staff are those as prescribed under Public Service Agreements. For further information, please follow the link: https://www.ucd.ie/hr/t4media/Academic%20Contract.pdf"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020178": {
      "title": "Research Accounts Assistant, UCD Research Finance Office, Temporary 18-month post",
      "description": "Research Accounts Assistant, UCD Research Finance Office, Temporary 18-month post Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Cúntóir Cuntais Taighde laistigh de Oifig Airgeadais Taighde UCD Cuirfidh sealbhóir an phoist tacaíocht riaracháin ar fáil laistigh den Oifig Airgeadais Taighde, agus déanfaidh siad réimse dualgas oibríochtúil agus airgeadais. I measc na bpríomhfhreagrachtaí, tá: coigeartuithe irisleabhair a ullmhú; réitigh chuntais bhainc a dhéanamh go tréimhsiúil; buiséid iarmharacha a fhíorú ar chuntais tionscadail le linn próiseála costais phá; agus taifid oifige a choinneáil. Beidh teagmháil phearsanta agus i scríbhinn le baill foirne acadúla agus tacaíochta agus le hionadaithe ó ghníomhaireachtaí seachtracha ina cuid shuntasach den ról. Scála Tuarastail: €32,856 - €49,419 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 04-11-2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Accounts Assistant within UCD Research Finance Office The post holder will be responsible for providing administrative support by carrying out various tasks and functions, including those of a financial nature, within the Research Finance Office. Duties will include: preparation of journal adjustments; periodic reconciliation of bank account; checking residual budgets on project accounts when processing pay costs; maintenance of files. Liaising with academic and support staff and representatives from external agencies in person and in writing will form a significant part of the role. 95 Executive Assistant_2013 (7911) Salary: €32,856 - €49,419 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 04-11-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020168": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 12 months",
      "description": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary 12 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Medicine. The purpose of this position is to support the development, manufacturing optimisation, and evaluation of clinical-grade injectable hydrogel kits, contributing to the research team's goals in biomaterials development and clinical translation. Working within the collaboration between UCD and Bláfar Ltd., the Research Assistant will support formulation studies, material characterisation, and the optimisation of purification, lyophilisation, and quality-control workflows. Under the direction of Professor Wenxin Wang and the supervision of senior researchers, the Research Assistant will carry out laboratory experiments, analyse data, and maintain experimental records and project documentation. The position also involves supporting laboratory operations, including instrument upkeep, consumable inventory, and health and safety compliance. Expected outputs include reliable experimental data, documented procedures, reproducible manufacturing workflows, and timely project reports. Salary Range: €34,129 - €44,311 Per Annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27/10/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020181": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary Up to 30 November 2027 (Part-Time 0.5 FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science, Temporary Up to 30 November 2027 (Part-Time 0.5 FTE) Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.5 FTE) post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Public Health, Physiotherapy and Sports Science. This is a research assistant position. This post supports the research activities related to a feasibility trial. The ExSCIP feasibility trial examines exoskeleton walking as a potential mechanistic-based intervention for neuropathic pain following spinal cord injury. It has a dose matched comparator of a relaxation intervention. Research activities include participant recruitment and screening, delivery of the exoskeleton intervention and data collation and liaison with the Centre for Support and Training in Analysis and Research (CSAR at UCD) and with a Health Economist collaborator. Fixed Salary: €34,129 Per Annum Pro Rata @0.5 FTE Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 06 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020188": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Research Assistant, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine Soft x-ray microscopy is a novel, exciting imaging technique which visualises cells in exquisite detail, but it has yet to be applied to imaging whole tissues. This project, which will be part of ERC Synergy Project NanoX, will develop techniques for CT-like imaging of 3D models of the liver and other organs. It will focus on hepatitis E virus, an emerging zoonotic disease with no specific treatments and no vaccine. This will allow us to visualise tissues at a level of detail not previously possible, a crucial step for understanding the mechanisms of disease. The project will benefit from the skillsets of international experts in infectious disease, physics and structural biology, with partners based at Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, Germany, and the University of Warwick, UK. See www.ucd.ie/nanox for further information. Salary Scale: €34,129 - €44,311 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 30-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020167": {
      "title": "Research Careers Development Officer, UCD Careers Network, Part-time temporary (0.5FTE) for 3 years (Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/11/2026 Research Careers Development Officer, UCD Careers Network, Part-time temporary (0.5FTE) for 3 years (Panel 12 months Permanent & Temporary) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Careers Development Officer within UCD Careers Network UCD Belfield Careers Network is a progressive careers centre based at the Belfield campus with a sister site at the Michael Smurfit Graduate Business School. Our enthusiastic team is passionate about student and researcher career development and employability, and we are now seeking a self-motivated and enthusiastic Research Careers Development Officer to join us and make a difference specifically to the Early Career Researcher experience at UCD. As the Research Careers Development Officer you will join the Research Careers Managers and Career & Skills Consultant (Graduate Researchers) to support both graduate research students and postdoctoral staff in their careers and skills development, ultimately so they can plan and develop careers in academia and across sectors in line with Impact 2030, Ireland’s Research and Innovation strategy. This will involve a strong level of organisational awareness, an understanding of the Research Careers Framework and a flexibility to work across units within UCD (e.g. Graduate Studies, UCD Research and HR People and Organisational development). Salary Scale: 95 Admin Officer Ii_2010 (0173_X) €52,519 - €67,129 (Pro rata at 0.5fte) Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 2 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach OIFIGEACH FORBARTHA GAIRMEACHA TAIGHDE laistigh de Líonra Gairmeacha UCD Is ionad gairme forásach é Líonra Gairmeacha Belfield UCD atá lonnaithe ar champas Belfield le comhsuíomh ag Scoil Iarchéime Ghnó Michael Smurfit. Tá ár bhfoireann dhíograiseach paiseanta faoi fhorbairt gairme agus infhostaitheacht mac léinn agus taighdeoirí agus táimid anois ag lorg OIFIGEACH FORBARTHA GAIRMEACHA TAIGHDE féinspreagtha agus díograiseach chun páirt a ghlacadh linn agus difríocht a dhéanamh go sonrach d'eispéireas an Taighdeora Luathghairme in UCD. Mar OIFIGEACH FORBARTHA GAIRMEACHA TAIGHDE, beidh tú ag obair le Bainisteoirí Gairmeacha Taighde agus sa Chomhairleoir Gairme agus Scileanna (Taighdeoirí Céime) chun tacú le mic léinn taighde iarchéime agus le baill foirne iardhochtúireachta araon ina ngairmeacha agus ina bhforbairt scileanna, ionas gur féidir leo ar deireadh gairmeacha sa saol acadúil agus ar fud earnálacha a phleanáil agus a fhorbairt i gcomhréir le Tionchar 2030, straitéis Taighde agus Nuálaíochta na hÉireann. Is éard a bheidh i gceist leis sin leibhéal láidir feasachta eagraíochta, tuiscint ar an gCreat Gairmeacha Taighde agus solúbthacht chun oibriú ar fud na n-aonad laistigh de UCD (e.g. Staidéar Iarchéime, Taighde UCD agus Daoine Acmhainní Daonna agus Forbairt Eagraíochtúil). 95 Admin Officer Ii_2010 (0173_X) Scála Tuarastail: €52,519 - €67,129 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 2.11.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020158": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, UCD School of Chemical & Bioprocess Engineering, Temporary 6 month post",
      "description": "Research Engineer, UCD School of Chemical & Bioprocess Engineering, Temporary 6 month post Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Engineer within UCD School of Chemical & Bioprocess Engineering This project is on the development of understanding and manipulation of how process-driven molecular simulation may be applied towards the design of nanobubbles and their controlled gas release, especially with a view towards acoustic perturbation. In terms of a proof-of-concept, a software suite will be developed to handle designed perturbations to nanobubbles with a view to assessing their controlled gas release. Building on Prof. English’s patented research, the common theme of applying external electric/magnetic fields to systems to bring about hydrate-formation phenomena will be explored and advanced in this research-engineer appointment at UCD. Fixed Salary: €52,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 28-10-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020170": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary part-time (0.6fte) appointment for 12 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Research Engineer, UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary part-time (0.6fte) appointment for 12 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Engineer within UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering NanoMind-GenAI is an ARC-ICT funded project on the development of a AI driven formulation and manufacturing software platform for lipid nanoparticles with the applications towards RNA therapeutics. NanoMind-GenAI will deliver an AI-driven decision-support platform that closes this gap. Combining agent-supported literature retrieval and interpretation with machine learning validated on over 3,000 LNP formulations, the platform will generate explainable, evidence-based formulation recommendations, supporting faster and more knowledge-grounded candidate prioritisation with traceable reasoning. Expected outputs include a tested software workflow, evidence-based candidate prioritisation methods, intensive customer discovery, product user specification and contributions to the project’s commercial development. Fixed Salary: €67,200 per annum pro-rata (i.e. Equal to €40,320 per annum part-time - at 0.6fte) Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27-Oct-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020190": {
      "title": "Research Finance Administrator, UCD Research Finance Office, Temporary 1 year post (with 9 month temporary panel)",
      "description": "Research Finance Administrator, UCD Research Finance Office, Temporary 1 year post (with 9 month temporary panel) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Finance Administrator within UCD Research Finance Office. The Finance Office is seeking to appoint a Research Finance Administrator to manage defined operational activities across the University’s post-award research financial management and compliance functions. Working under the supervision of a Research Agency Account Manager, the Administrative Officer is responsible for the post award financial management of all externally and internally funded research projects and ensuring compliance with funding terms and UCD policies. They are also responsible for developing and motivating staff to achieve predetermined individual and team objectives. The postholder will contribute to the accuracy of the University's research financial reporting, the quality of audit-ready documentation, and the continuous improvement of systems within the Research Finance function. Additionally, the Research Finance Administrator will be responsible for supervising team members, ensuring that tasks are delivered effectively and that staff are developed to meet the evolving needs of the research community. 95 Admin Officer Ii_2010 (0173_X) Salary Scale : €52,519 - € 67,129 per annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 20/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Riarthóir Airgeadais Taighde laistigh de Oifig Airgeadais Taighde UCD. Tacóidh an ceapaí leis an bhfeidhm Airgeadais Taighde trí thuairisciú airgeadais taighde beacht a chinntiú, cáipéisíocht atá réidh le haghaidh iniúchta a choinneáil, agus feabhsuithe leanúnacha córais a chur chun cinn. Ina theannta sin, beidh an Riarthóir Airgeadais Taighde freagrach as maoirseacht a dhéanamh ar bhaill foirne, ag cinntiú go ndéantar tascanna a chomhlíonadh go héifeachtach agus go bhforbraítear baill foirne chun freastal ar riachtanais athraitheacha phobal na taighde. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 20/11/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020189": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary Part-time (0.5 FTE) Until 30 September 2027",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Research Project Manager, UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Temporary Part-time (0.5 FTE) Until 30 September 2027 Applications are invited for a temporary part-time (0.5 FTE) post of a Research Project Manager within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering. The d-Lab: Digital Agriculture and Bioresource at the School of Biosystems and Food Engineering invites applications for a dynamic Research Project Manager. You will support the Principal Investigator Dr. Dimitrios Argyropoulos by managing large-scale, multi-partner EU funded projects on sustainable agri-food supply chains. You will oversee the daily management, ensuring efficient grant administration and timely reporting. Important Note for Applicants/Particular to this position: This is a Temporary part-time (i.e. half-time/0.5FTE) post until 30 September 2027. The hours of work for this post are equal to 19.5hrs per week (of a regular/full-time 39hr working week) - and the actual days and hours worked, will be as agreed with the Principal Investigator. Please note that this role will include travel across Europe. Fixed Salary: €45,000 Per Annum Pro Rata (i.e. €22,500 Per Annum @0.5FTE) Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 30 October 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020186": {
      "title": "Senior IT Specialist, School of Earth Sciences, Temporary 60 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/11/2026 Senior IT Specialist, School of Earth Sciences, Temporary 60 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior IT Specialist within the School of Earth Sciences UCD School of Earth Sciences seeks to recruit a senior IT systems administrator to support the day-to-day IT requirements of the School’s students, staff and research teams, to facilitate access to hardware and software, and to maintain and oversee the development and security of the School’s strategic IT infrastructure in collaboration with UCD IT services. The school runs its own secure network, HPC and general and storage server architecture and benefits from access to a wide range of licenced third-party software for 3D subsurface interpretation and modelling software, open-source and in-house software, and generic packages made available via UCD IT services. The IT administrator will provide expert and timely support for: (1) mainly (but not exclusively) Windows-based, office, classroom, field, and work stations, associated software; (2) specialist geoscience (geophysical, geospatial, geomodelling) and 3D interpretation software and associated hardware; (3) management of the School’s network, licenses, firewall and dedicated servers; (4) storage and off-site back-up facilities, and (5) classroom audio-visual and video-capture equipment. 95 Admin Officer I_2010 (0172_X) Salary Scale: €53,876 - €72,929 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 26 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Speisialtóir Sinsearach TF laistigh de Scoil na nDomhaneolaíochtaí Cuirtear fáilte roimh iarratais ar ról sealadach, téarma seasta, 5 bliana, mar Speisialtóir Sinsearach TF (Oifigeach Riaracháin I) laistigh de Scoil na nDomhaneolaíochtaí UCD Achoimre ar an bPost: I gcomhar le Seirbhísí TF UCD, tá Scoil na nDomhaneolaíochtaí UCD ag lorg riarthóir sinsearach córas TF. Déanfaidh an t-iarrthóir rathúil bonneagar lárnach TF na Scoile a bhainistiú, a fhorbairt agus a dhaingniú, rochtain ar chrua-earraí agus bogearraí riachtanacha a éascú, agus freastal ar riachtanais laethúla TF na mac léinn, na foirne agus na bhfoirne taighde. 95 Admin Officer I_2010 (0172_X) Scála Tuarastail: €53,876 - €72,929 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 26.11.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020180": {
      "title": "Social Media Executive, UCD Marketing and Communications - External Communication, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Social Media Executive, UCD Marketing and Communications - External Communication, Temporary Fixed Term 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Social Media Executive within UCD Marketing and Communications - External Communication. The External Communication Team within the Marketing and Communications Unit leads on strategic and critical communication to promote and protect the university and its mission. It provides professional communication support to the president, the university management team, faculty and other senior campus leaders. Its specialist team communicates strategically, through the most effective channels and the most impactful formats and styles, to inform, engage and inspire external stakeholders in support of the university and its strategic goals. Its work includes, inter alia, media relations, news writing, speech writing, op-ed writing, thought-leadership opportunities, digital and social content, communication counsel, training, and outreach to all key external audiences. We are seeking outstanding candidates with proven experience in social media channel development and audience growth through publishing engaging, high-quality social media content informed by data insights at a fast-paced and progressive company/organisation. 95 Admin Officer I_2010 (0172_X) Salary Scale: €53,876 - €72,929 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Feidhmeannach Meán Sóisialta laistigh de Margaíocht agus Cumarsáid - Cumarsáid Sheachtrach. Tá an Fhoireann Cumarsáide Seachtraí laistigh den Aonad Margaíochta agus Cumarsáide i gceannas ar chumarsáid straitéiseach agus chriticiúil chun an ollscoil agus a misean a chur chun cinn agus a chosaint. Cuireann sé tacaíocht chumarsáide ghairmiúil ar fáil don Uachtarán, d’Fhoireann Bainistíochta na hOllscoile, don fhoireann acadúil agus do cheannairí sinsearacha eile ar an gcampas. Déanann a fhoireann speisialtóireachta cumarsáid straitéiseach, trí na bealaí is éifeachtaí agus na formáidí agus na stíleanna is mó tionchair, chun geallsealbhóirí seachtracha a chur ar an eolas agus a spreagadh chun tacú leis an ollscoil agus lena spriocanna straitéiseacha. I measc na bpríomhfhreagrachtaí, tá caidreamh leis na meáin, bailiú nuachta, dréachtú óráidí agus alt tuairime, seasamh ceannaireachta smaointeoireachta, cruthú na meán digiteach agus sóisialta, comhairleoireacht chumarsáide straitéisí, oiliúint, agus rannpháirtíocht spriocdhírithe i measc lucht féachana seachtrach príomhúil. Táimid ag lorg iarrthóirí den scoth a bhfuil taithí léirithe acu maidir leis na meáin shóisialta a fhorbairt agus lucht féachana a leathnú. Cruthóidh agus foilseoidh an t-iarrthóir idéalach ábhar mealltach den chéad scoth atá bunaithe ar léargais sonraí laistigh de thimpeallacht dhinimiciúil, réamhbhreathnaitheach. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 12 Mí na Samhna 2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020169": {
      "title": "Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor paediatrics - CHI at Temple Street Crumlin, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary Specified Purpose circa 6-9 Months, Maternity Leave cover",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor paediatrics - CHI at Temple Street Crumlin, UCD School of Medicine, Temporary Specified Purpose circa 6-9 Months, Maternity Leave cover Applications are invited for a specified purpose post of a Special Lecturer Clinical Tutor paediatrics - CHI at Temple Street Crumlin within UCD School of Medicine The Special Lecturers/Clinical Tutors play a major role in supporting, organizing and delivering clinical teaching for our students on rotation in our affiliated Teaching hospitals. The Clinical Tutors instruct and supervise students during their clinical attachment, provide lectures and tutorials as part of the formal clinical curriculum and assist with the preparation of clinical examinations. They provide academic support and career mentoring to students and ensure that the clinical rotation supports the learning objective of the relevant module. Special Lec/Clinical Tutor_2010 (0081_X) Salary Scale: €70,276 - €82,756 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 03-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020184": {
      "title": "Student Counsellor Intern, UCD Student Counselling Service, Temporary 12 month post (Full-time)",
      "description": "Student Counsellor Intern, UCD Student Counselling Service, Temporary 12 month post (Full-time) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Student Counsellor Intern within UCD Student Counselling Service. The Student Counselling Service wishes to recruit an Intern Student Counsellor to join our team of Student Counsellors and deliver counselling and mental health expertise to the University, under supervision. The focus of this post is the provision of high-quality psychological therapy, 1:1 and with groups. This post will suit a newly qualified psychotherapist, counselling/clinical psychologist seeking to build hours to fulfil professional accreditation/registration requirements. Fixed Scale: €35,000 per annum . Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Intéirneach Comhairleora Mac Léinn laistigh de Seirbhís Chomhairleoireachta Mac Léinn UCD. Is mian le Seirbhís Chomhairleoireachta Mac Léinn UCD Intéirneach Comhairleora Mac Léinn a earcú, chun tacú leis an bhfoireann saineolas maidir le sláinte meabhrach agus seirbhísí comhairleoireachta a chur ar fáil ar fud na hOllscoile, faoi mhaoirseacht. Is é fócas an phoist seo ná teiripe shíceolaíoch ardchaighdeáin a sholáthar, duine le duine agus le grúpaí. Beidh an post seo oiriúnach do shíciteiripeoir, comhairleoir/síceolaí cliniciúil nuacháilithe atá ag iarraidh na huaireanta cliniciúla riachtanacha a charnadh le haghaidh clárúcháin agus creidiúnaithe gairmiúla. Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 12/11/2026. Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020182": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 March 2028",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, School of Biosystems and Food Engineering, Fixed-term post until 31 March 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of Biosystems and Food Engineering The BioAssess Project, funded by Sustainable Energy Authority Ireland and the Department of Agriculture, Food and the Marine, aims to provide a novel framework which assess the environmental, economic and social impacts of the use of biomass for bioenergy and in the bioeconomy in Ireland. The framework will identify any unintended consequences of the use of biomass in different sectors and will inform industry, local authorities and policymakers on how to develop schemes and policies for the sustainable use of biomass. BioAssess will engage with key stakeholders through the Industry Advisory panel including members from industry (energy and farming), local authorities and policymakers, and through project workshops (e.g. farmers, foresters, bioenergy processors, bioeconomy companies etc.) to ensure uptake of the BioAssess framework. BioAssess is led by University College Dublin, with collaborators University of Galway and Munster Technological University. Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 05-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020166": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 x 2, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Temporary 30 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 x 2, UCD School of Civil Engineering, Temporary 30 months Applications are invited for two temporary posts of UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Civil Engineering. SYN-Bridge (Synchronized Mobile and Stationary Sensor Networks for Real-Time Bridge Health Assessment) is a 36-month US–Ireland R&D Partnership project between University College Dublin, Queen’s University Belfast and a partner university in the United States. The UCD component is funded by Research Ireland. The project combines measurements from instrumented vehicles with stationary sensors on the bridge to produce reliable indicators of bridge condition. The posts exist to deliver UCD’s contribution to Work Package 1, Development and Testing of Damage Detection Algorithms, which UCD leads. Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the postholders will develop, test, and validate methods for assessing bridge condition, moving from numerical simulation through laboratory validation to field trials with project partners. The work will initially cover damage detection and the identification of vehicle loads, together with the probabilistic assessment of detection reliability and digital-twin modelling; the allocation of work between the two posts will depend on the expertise of the appointees and on how the research develops. Expected outcomes are validated methods, contributions to shared project datasets and peer-reviewed publications. Fixed Salary: €47,273 Per Annum Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020193": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 2 Years (Start Date: 01 Feb 2027)",
      "description": "Research Assistant, UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Temporary Fixed Term 2 Years (Start Date: 01 Feb 2027) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Assistant within UCD School of Veterinary Medicine. University College Dublin is seeking a Research Assistant to join a large multi-disciplinary research team focusing on nutrition and health solutions as part of an innovation programme focussed on transforming food waste into functional ingredients. The research will involve conducting in vitro (Caco-2) studies to examine the effect of fermented and non-fermented upcycled food ingredients on gut health. The successful candidate will be involved in supporting the assessment of a pipeline of ingredients for gut health and liaising with the wider research community on the selection of the best ingredient to be brought forward for assessment in a human intervention study. Salary Range: €34,129 - €41,501 Per Annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 03/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020192": {
      "title": "Technical Officer, School of Veterinary Medicine, Veterinary Biosciences Section, Permanent",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Technical Officer, School of Veterinary Medicine, Veterinary Biosciences Section, Permanent Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Technical Officer within the School of Veterinary Medicine The UCD School of Veterinary Medicine, Veterinary Biosciences Section is recruiting a Technical Officer to join the existing team members supporting teaching and research in Veterinary Anatomy. The role will be based in the Anatomy Dissection areas and provide technical support to academics delivering dissection classes for modules in the veterinary and veterinary nursing programs as well as technical, administrative and training support to the laboratories in the section. Duties include specimen sourcing, development and maintenance, maintaining the anatomy area, class set up and clear up as well as assisting in research activities and teaching sessions. The successful candidate will be expected to take a lead role in technical support in these areas, keeping abreast of technical developments and adapting to new technologies. The role also includes supporting the School’s Body Donor Programme and driving UCD vehicles. The candidate should be enthusiastic, demonstrate initiative, have a conscientious work ethic and a methodical approach 95 Technical Officer_2013 (7915) Salary Range: €48,239 - €63,177 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 10 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Oifigeach Teicniúil laistigh de Scoil an Leighis Tréidliachta Cuirtear fáilte roimh iarratais don phost mar oifigeach teicniúil leis an Rannóg Bitheolaíochtaí Tréidliachta laistigh de Scoil an Leighis Tréidliachta UCD. Beidh an té a cheapfar ag tacú le teagasc agus taighde san Anatamaíocht Tréidliachta. Díríonn an ról ar Dhioscadh Anatamaíochta agus cuirfidh an ceapaí tacaíocht theicniúil ar fáil don fhoireann teagaisc, a chuireann ranganna diosctha ar fáil don chláir tréidliachta agus altranais tréidliachta. Freisin, cuirfidh siad tacaíocht theicniúil, riaracháin, agus oiliúna do na saotharlanna sa rannóg. I measc na bhfreagrachtaí, beidh ar an gceapaí: samplaí a aimsiú, a fhorbairt agus chothú, limistéar anatamaíochta a chothú, ranganna a ullmhú agus a ghlanadh ranganna, agus cúnamh a thabhairt i ngníomhaíochtaí taighde agus i seisiúin teagaisc. Beifear ag súil go nglacfaidh an t-iarrthóir rathúil ról ceannaireachta maidir le tacaíocht theicniúil a sholáthar sna réimsí seo, ag coinneáil suas chun dáta le forbairtí teicniúla agus ag dul i dtaithí ar theicneolaíochtaí nua. Áirítear leis an ról freisin, tacú le Clár Deontóirí Coirp na Scoile agus feithiclí UCD a thiomáint. Ní mór don cheapaí bheith díograiseach, bheith toilteanach obair a stuaim féin, eitic oibre coinsiasach a léiriú, agus cur chuige rianúil a bheith acu. 95 Technical Officer_2013 (7915) Scála Tuarastail: €48,239 - €63,177 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 10.11.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020194": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD Teaching and Learning, Temporary 12 Months (fixed term)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 17/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD Teaching and Learning, Temporary 12 Months (fixed term) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD Teaching and Learning UCD Teaching and Learning is seeking to appoint a Postdoctoral Researcher to support delivery of the Generative AI in Teaching & Learning work package, a core strand of the Strategic Engagement – Learning for Life initiative arising from UCD Strategy 2030: Breaking Boundaries. This 12-month post is funded through the strategic UCD General Education project, AI and Digital Skills strand (https://www.ucd.ie/registrar/ucdstrategicpoliciesandinitatives/ucdgeneraleducation/) Working closely with UCD Teaching and Learning and in close contact with the General Education Academic Advisory Group, the successful candidate will conduct desk-based research into the pedagogical, ethical, and practical implications of Generative AI for teaching, learning, and assessment; contribute to and, where appropriate, lead research initiatives engaging faculty and students on GenAI-related themes; design and deliver workshops for academic and professional staff; and liaise across Colleges, Schools, and central units to help shape institutional conversation and policy development on Teaching & Learning in the age of GenAI. PD1 Salary Range: €47,273 - €53,925 per annum PD2 Salary Range: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 17 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020195": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Law, Temporary up to 31st December 2028",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Law, Temporary up to 31st December 2028 Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Law. UCD seeks to appoint a Post-doctoral Researcher (PDR) for RIGHTS-TO-UNITE, a research project funded by an ERC Advanced Grant led by Prof Dagmar Schiek. The position is due to start on 18 January 2027. Although this is a full-time position, applications for part-time arrangements are also welcome, and we will endeavour to accommodate such requests. The RIGHTS-TO-UNITE Project aims to generate a new socio-legal theory of European integration based on citizens’ experience of European integration through rights, and to explore its viability through qualitative research using liberal/economic, social and digital rights as fields of research. Its multi-level comparison encompasses smaller states in the EU and its neighbourhood, more specifically four EU countries (Ireland, Czech Republic, Greece and Sweden) and four neighbourhood states (Northern Ireland, Norway, North Macedonia and Georgia). The qualitative comparison uses expert interviews to identify barriers and enablers of using EU-derived rights as well as the experts’ assessment of how practical the intended effects may be. In a second step, lay-persons perception of and experience with EU-derived rights are explored by using visualised scenarios potentially relevant for the usage of economic/liberal, social and/or digital rights derived from EU Treaties or Association Agreements. Focus groups will be conducted as citizens’ meetings mimicking citizens’ assemblies. The PDR joins the project in its fourth year, complementing the team consisting of the Principal Investigator, a post-doctoral researcher, three research associates, three PhD researchers and a research project manager (part-time). For this Post-doctoral Researcher position , we are looking for a highly motivated and qualified researcher with a strong profile in European Studies (sociology, legal studies, political science, industrial relations or another relevant field). The candidate must have experience in qualitative comparative research, such as focus groups and expert interviews, and an understanding of socio-legal comparison. You will be academically fluent in English, and familiar with the most important theories of European integration, including those focusing on integration through law and the role of rights. Excellent academic communication skills are essential. While the working language of the project is English, additional knowledge of any of the languages of the target countries of our project will be an advantage. As part of an international team, you will collaborate with the advisory board (one member for each comparative countries) and external service providers. Salary Range: €47,273 - €47,879 Per Annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 09/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020197": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of English, Drama and Film, 3 years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2, UCD School of English, Drama and Film, 3 years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or 2 within UCD School of English, Drama and Film. Applications are invited for a full-time, three-year postdoctoral fellowship to join a team working on a European Research Council-funded project entitled ‘Anticolonialism, Pan-Asianism, and Periodical Culture in Southeast Asia, c. 1850-1920’ (PanAsia). Spanning three European empires (French, British, and Dutch) and five interconnected port cities (Singapore, Penang, Rangoon, Batavia, and Saigon), PanAsia is a five-year (2027-2032) study of the newspapers, journals, and magazines of nineteenth and early twentieth-century Southeast Asia (c. 1850-1920). The project’s primary objectives are, first, to compare the production of anticolonial periodical media by colonised peoples in multiple languages across the five maritime sites; second, to uncover transimperial and/or transnational print networks of anticolonial resistance between colonised peoples across the region; and third, to investigate how pan-Asian or shared Asian cultural values were used to mobilise anticolonial thinking and praxis. In its first stage, PanAsia will focus on a) locating the relevant multilingual periodical corpus and obtaining permissions to publish or republish that corpus on the project website; b) designing and implementing a searchable and machine-readable database of relevant parts of the corpus; c) identifying and cross-referencing intertextual exchange within the corpus; d) identifying reprinted and/or syndicated articles across the corpus; and e) identifying periodical fiction across the corpus. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum PD2 Salary: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 18 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020206": {
      "title": "Administrator, Governance, Tax and Treasury, Finance Office, Temporary 2-year post",
      "description": "Administrator, Governance, Tax and Treasury, Finance Office, Temporary 2-year post Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Riarthóir – Rialachas, Cáin & Cistíocht laistigh de Oifig Airgeadais UCD Is mian le hOifig Airgeadais UCD Riarthóir – Rialachas, Cáin agus Cistíocht a earcú chun tacaíocht oibríochtúil laethúil a sholáthar i réimsí riaracháin chánach, oibríochtaí cistíochta, agus rialachais airgeadais. Scála Tuarastail: €46,703 - €56,831 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 12/11/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Administrator – Governance, Tax & Treasury within UCD Finance Office The Finance Office is seeking to appoint an Administrator – Governance, Tax and Treasury to provide day-to-day operational support in the areas of tax administration, treasury operations, and financial governance. Reporting to the Senior Administrator – Governance, Tax and Treasury, the postholder will support administrative and financial tasks such as document preparation, data entry, record-keeping, reconciliations, and compliance tracking. The role plays a key part in maintaining high-quality financial documentation and supporting the delivery of tax returns, bank reconciliations, and month-end procedures. 95 Senior Executive Assistant_2010 Salary Scale: €46,703 - €56,831 per annum. Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12/11/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020200": {
      "title": "Chief Technical Officer II, UCD School of Mechanical & Materials Engineering, Permanent, 12 Month Panel",
      "description": "Chief Technical Officer II, UCD School of Mechanical & Materials Engineering, Permanent, 12 Month Panel Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post buan Príomhoifigeach Teicniúil II laistigh de Innealtóireacht Mheicniúil agus Ábhar Baineann na gníomhaíochtaí teagaisc, taighde agus nuálaíochta laistigh de Scoil na hInnealtóireachta Meicniúla agus Ábhar UCD le teicneolaíochtaí atá ag athrú go leanúnach agus réimse leathan de threalamh caighdeánach tionscail chomh maith le trealamh, comhpháirteanna agus córais thurgnamhacha saincheaptha. Beidh an post seo mar Phríomhoifigeach Teicniúil II lonnaithe i Saotharlanna Teagaisc na Scoile agus oibreoidh sé (i gcomhairle) leis an bhfoireann acadúil agus theicniúil, i ndearadh, tógáil, suiteáil agus cothabháil threalamh saotharlainne teagaisc na Scoile, lena n-áirítear i Spás Déantóra nua na Scoile agus i saotharlanna fochéime na Scoile a bhíonn ar siúl in Ionad Foghlama O’Connor. Áirítear leis sin trealamh meicniúil, gaireas, innealra gaolmhar agus páirteanna gaolmhara, chomh maith le gníomhaíochtaí tacaíochta gaolmhara éagsúla eile. Éileoidh an ról freisin tacú le gníomhaíochtaí taighde turgnamhaigh na Scoile, i gcás inar gá. Scála Tuarastail: €73,544 - €90,326 per annum in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 12/11/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a permanent post of a Chief Technical Officer II within UCD School of Mechanical & Materials Engineering The teaching, research, and innovation activities within the UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering involve continuously evolving technologies and a wide variety of industry standard equipment as well as customised equipment, components, and experimental systems. This post of Chief Technical Officer II will be based in the School’s Teaching Laboratories and will work (in consultation) with academic and technical staff, in the design, construction, installation and maintenance of the School’s teaching laboratory equipment, including in the School’s new Maker Space and the School’s undergraduate laboratories that take place in the O’Connor Centre for Learning. This includes mechanical equipment, apparatus, related machinery and parts, as well as in various other associated support activities. The role will also require supporting the School’s experimental research activities, where required. 95 Chief Technical Officer (CTOII)_2010 Salary Scale: €73,544 - €90,326 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12/11/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020207": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 30 months",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2, UCD School of Earth Sciences, 30 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 or Level 2 within School of Earth Sciences. The UCD School of Earth Sciences is seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher to contribute to TabPhish, a five-year research project funded by a European Research Council (ERC) Starting Grant. The project aims to develop and apply innovative geochemical tracer methods to improve our understanding of human impacts on groundwater systems over decadal to centennial timescales. TabPhish is particularly focused on long-term changes in the sources and fate of nitrogen in groundwater systems along with water-table depth. The successful candidate will undertake research involving the development and application of dissolved gas isotope analytical techniques, laboratory experiments, groundwater field sampling, and quantitative interpretation of geochemical data. The role will involve contributing to the development of new analytical capabilities at UCD, designing and conducting research investigations, and collaborating with national and international research partners. The position will also provide opportunities to conduct laboratory research at collaborating institutions, particularly Heidelberg University in Germany. PD1 Salary: €47,273 - €53,925 Per Annum; * PD2 Salary: €55,399 - €60,250 Per Annum * Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 15/01/2027. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead. The PD2 post is intended for researchers that have completed PD1. As with the PD1, if you have already completed your PD2 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD2, or your total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 6 years, you should not apply and should refer to Research Fellow posts instead."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020203": {
      "title": "Senior Data Scientist, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Initial 4-month contract with possibility of extension",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Senior Data Scientist, UCD School of Computer Science - CeADAR, Initial 4-month contract with possibility of extension Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior Data Scientist within the School of Computer Science CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. We are very passionate about applying ML algorithms and develop AI applied research and innovation solutions using from classic ML to novel transformer neural networks. We test and measure the real customer impact of each model we deploy and support the ecosystem with training, advisory, and AI infrastructure. CeADAR is seeking an experienced individual who has a demonstrated successful track record in applied data science. Salary Range: €65,000 - €88,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 5 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020205": {
      "title": "Senior Data Scientist, UCD School of Computer Science / CeADAR, 24 months",
      "description": "Senior Data Scientist, UCD School of Computer Science / CeADAR, 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior Data Scientist within UCD School of Computer Science / CeADAR. Applications are invited for the role of Senior Data Scientist in CeADAR Ireland’s Centre for Applied AI. CeADAR is funded by the Irish government via Enterprise Ireland and the IDA and is based in University College Dublin. As the national centre for applied artificial intelligence, CeADAR’s mission is to help industry and the public sector to adopt AI. In addition, CeADAR is also the designated European Digital Innovation Hub for AI in Ireland, and has a strong presence in the European RD&I landscape. See www.ceadar.ie for further details. We are very passionate about applying ML algorithms and develop AI applied research and innovation solutions using classic ML to novel transformer neural networks. We test and measure the real customer impact of each model we deploy and support the ecosystem with training, advisory, and AI infrastructure. CeADAR is seeking an experienced individual who will support applied research projects and who have a demonstrated successful track record in data science in industrial research settings (>6 years). Salary range: €65,000 to €88,000 per annum. Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 05/11/2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020199": {
      "title": "Senior Energy Policy Researcher, School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, 3 Years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Senior Energy Policy Researcher, School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, 3 Years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior Energy Policy Researcher within UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Ireland’s energy system is undergoing a profound transformation as electrification is set to accelerate across transport, heating, and industry. This shift, combined with the rapid expansion of energy-intensive data centres, is reshaping electricity demand and supply patterns. The transition is occurring in the context of the national Climate Action Plan targets, EU energy market reforms, and the urgent need to achieve sustained reductions in greenhouse gas emissions This post will develop a comprehensive AC power flow model of the Irish transmission grid to support long-term system planning. The model will form part of an integrated energy system analysis framework aligned with SEAI’s national energy modelling efforts. Using detailed network topology, generation and demand data, and spatial load projections, the model will simulate the grid’s technical performance under multiple future energy scenarios. It will quantify the grid reinforcements, operational flexibility, and system services required to achieve Ireland’s renewable energy and emissions targets. Salary: €55,000 – €75,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12-Nov-2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020201": {
      "title": "Senior RF/mmWave IC Design Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Senior RF/mmWave IC Design Engineer, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior RF/mmWave IC Design Engineer within UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering. This technical leadership role exists to direct the engineering execution, layout synthesis, and final top-level integration of a sub-THz transceiver SoC. Operating within UCD's deep-tech commercialization framework, the appointee translates project milestones into scalable silicon architectures. The position serves as a principal coordinator across cross-functional RF, analog, digital, and test teams, ensuring technical synchronization and design integrity. Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the appointee maintains primary technical accountability for block-level circuit delivery, floorplanning, and layout supervision. Key responsibilities include establishing sign-off methodologies and defining comprehensive post-silicon validation frameworks to deliver tape-out-ready components optimized to anchor an early-stage deep-tech startup venture. The mmWave TRx project, funded under an Enterprise Ireland Commercialisation Fund programme, is focused on the development of a highly integrated sub-THz transceiver SoC for next-generation communication and sensing applications. The project combines cutting-edge RFIC design, antenna integration, and silicon validation, with the definitive objective of creating robust technology suitable for a future venture-backed spin-out company. Salary Range: €65,000 - €80,000 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020202": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Officer (Mechanical Testing), UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 5 year post, 12 Months Panel",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Senior Technical Officer (Mechanical Testing), UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, Temporary 5 year post, 12 Months Panel Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior Technical Officer (Mechanical Testing) within the School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering The teaching, research and innovation activities within the UCD School of Mechanical and Materials Engineering involve a continually changing and a wide variety of customised equipment, components and experimental systems. The post of Senior Technical Officer will be based in both the Materials Mechanical Testing Areas and Manufacturing workshop and will work (in consultation) with staff, postgraduate and undergraduate students in materials testing and, in the design, construction, installation and repair of mechanical equipment and apparatus and related machinery, and in various other associated support activities, as required. The post-holder will also manufacture routine and bespoke items of equipment for both research and teaching laboratories. The workshop is equipped with lathes, CNC milling machines, CNC Lathe, EDM, TIG, MIG, MMA, Guillotines, Drilling Machines, Benders, Band Saws, Grinding Wheels, and Welding Equipment. The successful candidate will have significant industrial experience of materials testing and in the use of CNC milling machines, CNC lathes and EDM processing. 95 Snr Technical Officer_2013 (7916) Salary Scale: €56,806 - €75,905 per annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 12 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadac Oifigeach Teicniúil Sinsearach (Tástáil Mheicniúil) laistigh de Innealtóireacht Mheicniúil agus Ábhar Baineann na gníomhaíochtaí teagaisc, taighde agus nuálaíochta laistigh de Scoil na hInnealtóireachta Meicniúla agus Ábhar UCD le réimse leathan de threalamh, comhpháirteanna agus córais thurgnamhacha atá ag athrú go leanúnach. Beidh post an Oifigigh Theicniúil Shinsearaigh lonnaithe sna Limistéir Tástála Meicniúla Ábhar agus sa cheardlann Déantúsaíochta araon agus oibreoidh sé (i gcomhairle) leis an bhfoireann, le mic léinn iarchéime agus le mic léinn fochéime i dtástáil ábhar agus, i ndearadh, tógáil, suiteáil agus deisiú trealaimh mheicniúil agus gairis mheicniúil agus innealra ghaolmhair, agus i ngníomhaíochtaí tacaíochta gaolmhara éagsúla eile, de réir mar is gá. Déanfaidh an sealbhóir poist gnáth-mhíreanna trealaimh agus sainmhíreanna trealaimh a mhonarú freisin do shaotharlanna taighde agus teagaisc araon. Tá an cheardlann feistithe le deileanna, meaisíní muilleoireachta CNC, Lathe CNC, EDM, TIG, MIG, MMA, Gilitíní, Meaisíní Druileála, Lúbairí, Crios-Sábha, Rothaí Meilt, agus Trealamh Rámhraitheora. Beidh taithí thionsclaíoch shuntasach ag an iarrthóir rathúil ar thástáil ábhar agus ar úsáid meaisíní muilleoireachta CNC, deileanna CNC agus próiseáil EDM. 95 Snr Technical Officer_2013 (7916) Scála Tuarastail: €56,806 - €75,905 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 12.11.2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020198": {
      "title": "UCD Research Fellow, UCD School of Chemistry_ CBNI, Temporary 24 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 UCD Research Fellow, UCD School of Chemistry_ CBNI, Temporary 24 months Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Research Fellow, within the School of Chemistry. CBNI, University College Dublin is seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow with research background in relevant areas of molecular and cellular biology to join a dynamic team dedicated to advancing the understanding and implementation of diagnostics and therapeutics at the nanoscale. The successful candidate will be specialized in molecular biological skills as well as being capable of interfacing with those (inside and outside) the laboratory driving new biologically relevant methodologies (single–cell sequencing, massive arrays HCA, CRISPR, cell libraries etc). As such, demonstrated experience in mammalian cell culture, advanced molecular biology and biochemistry techniques such as ChIP-sequencing, CRISPR, flow cytometry and live cell microscopy is highly desirable. The successful candidate will work to develop, adapt and optimise workflows. The purpose of the role is to deliver a specific research project. The role allows the Research Fellow the professional development opportunity to demonstrate the capacity for independent and self-directed research and scholarship and the management of a research team. The role allows the Fellow to assemble a portfolio of independent achievement and render themselves competitive for tenured academic positions or senior scientific roles in industry. Research Fellow Salary: €67,214 - €69,163 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 5 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020211": {
      "title": "Information Compliance Support Officer, Freedom of Information Office UCD Corporate and Legal, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years",
      "description": "Information Compliance Support Officer, Freedom of Information Office UCD Corporate and Legal, Temporary Fixed Term 5 years Tugtar cuireadh d'iarratais ar post sealadach Oifigeach Tacaíochta Comhlíonta Faisnéise laistigh de An Oifig um Shaoráil Faisnéise (Corparáideach & Dlí UCD) Is é feidhm an Aonaid ná a chinntiú go gcomhlíonann an Ollscoil go hiomlán na hoibleagáidí reachtúla atá uirthi faoin Acht um Shaoráil Faisnéise (SF) 2014 agus faoi na Rialacháin maidir le Rochtain ar Fhaisnéis faoin gComhshaol (RF) 2007 – 2018. Chomh maith leis sin, cuireann an tAonad treoir ar fáil don institiúid maidir le taifid ollscoile a bhainistiú, i gcomhréir leis na caighdeáin dhlíthiúla a bhaineann leis an Saoráil Faisnéise agus leis an Rochtain ar Fhaisnéis faoin gComhshaol. Scála Tuarastail: €53,876 - €72,929 in aghaidh na bliana Déanfar an ceapachán ar scála agus de réir threoirlínte na Roinne Airgeadais Dáta dúnta: 12:00 uair (am áitiúil na hÉireann) ar 27/11/2026 Ní mór iarratas a bheith istigh faoin am agus dáta atá sonraithe. Déanfar aon iarratas atá fós ar siúl ag an am dúnta 12:00 uair (Am Áitiúil na hÉireann) ar an dáta dúnta sonraithe a scriosadh go huathoibríoch ag an gcóras. Ní féidir le UCD glacadh le hiarratais dhéanacha. Níl cúnamh ag teastáil ó UCD ó Ghníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta. Seolfar ar ais aon CV a chuir na Gníomhaireachtaí Earcaíochta isteach. Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Information Compliance Support Officer within Freedom of Information Office (UCD Corporate & Legal) The functions of the Unit are to ensure organisational compliance with the University’s obligations under the Freedom of Information Act (FOI) 2014 and the Access to Information on the Environment Regulations (AIE) 2007 - 2018. Its role is also to advise the university in the management of university records in accordance with the FOI/AIE legislation. 95 Admin Officer I_2010 Salary Scale: €53,876 - €72,929 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 27/11/2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020210": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Grass and Forage Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary specified purpose contract to cover maternity leave, estimated duration 9 months",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Grass and Forage Science, UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, Temporary specified purpose contract to cover maternity leave, estimated duration 9 months Applications are invited for a specified purpose) post of a Lecturer/Assistant Professor in Grass and Forage Science within the School of Agriculture & Food Science This role, based in the UCD School of Agriculture & Food Science, will support undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, and wider engagement in sustainable grass and forage production for environmentally resilient and economically viable food systems. The appointee will join a dynamic and interdisciplinary team of 18 full-time academics within the Section of Animal & Crop Science, contributing to a shared mission of addressing global food, environmental, and societal challenges through teaching, research, and knowledge exchange in animal and crop production systems. We are seeking a highly motivated individual with a demonstrated passion for teaching and research in grassland and forage systems, especially in the context of sustainable agriculture and food systems. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in Agricultural Science or a closely related discipline, with a strong focus on grassland/forage science and ideally with research interests that intersect with environmental sustainability, livestock production systems, climate adaptation and soil health. In addition to a strong research profile, the appointee should demonstrate excellent communication, organisational and interpersonal skills and a commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. The role will involve meaningful contributions to School and University initiatives that support the transition to more sustainable food systems, including climate-smart agriculture, biodiversity conservation, and sustainable land use. 95 Lecturer/Asst Professor Above The Bar (7943) Salary Scale: €66,055 - €104,600 Per Annum Appointment will be made on scale and in accordance with the Department of Finance guidelines Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020209": {
      "title": "Senior Energy Policy Researcher, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 3 Years",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Senior Energy Policy Researcher, UCD School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Temporary 3 Years Applications are invited for a temporary post of a Senior Energy Policy Researcher within the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Investments in future generation and storage assets can be strongly influenced by their potential location. Being subject to resource potential, environmental constraints, social acceptance and planning frameworks, the determination of plausible sites for power and energy assets is multi-faceted and typically asset specific. However, it is not always typical for long-term system planning models to consider how locational aspects affect a candidate investment asset’s resource potential, cost or return on investment, as well as the knock-on implications for the wider system. Furthermore, non-consideration of spatial constraints can hide potential land-use conflicts. This post will develop comprehensive spatial datasets for a set of key future power and energy technologies in Ireland and automated workflow routines to explore how these spatial considerations affect long-term decarbonisation pathways for Ireland’s power system using Spine tools. The model will form part of an integrated energy system analysis framework aligned with SEAI’s national energy modelling efforts. Salary Range: €55,000 – €75,000 per annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 November 2026 Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CV's submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned."
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/ucdrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=020208": {
      "title": "UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Agriculture and Food Science - Animal and Crop Sciences, Temporary 24 months (04 Jan 2027 - 03 Jan 2029)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1, UCD School of Agriculture and Food Science - Animal and Crop Sciences, Temporary 24 months (04 Jan 2027 - 03 Jan 2029) Applications are invited for a temporary post of a UCD Post-doctoral Research Fellow Level 1 within UCD School of Agriculture and Food Science - Animal and Crop Sciences. This position is funded by HERDPATH, an ERC Starting Grant project investigating how livestock and their pathogens have co-evolved over the last 10,000 years. The successful candidate will lead the deep analysis of livestock genomes – principally sheep and goat, drawing on data from other domesticates – generated from archaeological remains across Eurasia and spanning the Neolithic to the present day. Working with these millennia-spanning genomic transects alongside large modern reference panels, the role centres on reconstructing demographic history, detecting and dating signatures of selection, and characterising how host genetic variation has responded to pathogen pressure since domestication. The successful candidate will apply and develop population genetic approaches suited to time-series and low-coverage ancient data, apply demographic approaches to reveal fluctuations in population size through time, and perform selection analyses to determine the interplay between evolution and demography during domestication history. Experience of inbreeding inference, demographic analyses, and selection inference are highly advantageous. Salary Range: €47,273 - €47,879 Per Annum Appointment on the above range will be dependent upon qualifications and experience. Closing date: 12:00 noon (local Irish time) on 13 November 2026. Applications must be submitted by the closing date and time specified. Any applications which are still in progress at the closing time of 12:00 noon (Local Irish Time) on the specified closing date will be cancelled automatically by the system. UCD are unable to accept late applications. UCD do not require assistance from Recruitment Agencies. Any CVs submitted by Recruitment Agencies will be returned. The PD1 position is intended for early-stage researchers, either just after completion of a PhD or for someone entering a new area for the first time. If you have already completed your PD1 stage in UCD or will soon complete a PD1, or you are an external applicant whose total Postdoctoral experience, inclusive of the duration of the advertised post, would exceed 4 years, you should not apply and should refer to PD2 posts instead."
    }
  },
